                "limitations": "Scope limited to the single assertion about /tmp/rejected-relative after user_config_dir with XDG_CONFIG_HOME='rejected-relative', ensure_exists=True, HOME=/tmp/fixture-home. The proposed unix.py rejects the relative value (os.path.isabs check) and falls back to expanduser('~/.config'), so _append_app_name_and_version/_optionally_create_directory only create /tmp/fixture-home/.config/demo/2, never /tmp/rejected-relative. The assertion does not contradict the requirement ('Never create a directory from a rejected relative value'), and the reference does not create the rejected directory. No wrong repair found within this scope; other paths/APIs excluded per instructions."
